 John if you would  please at reporting that there was a  group of Liz trust supporting hedge fund  managers who attended a dinner a week  ago every one of them was shorting the  pan which means that you know but for  the benefit of others who perhaps don't  they were betting that it would go much  lower against the dollar the paper  reported several of them made small  fortunes shorting the pound the  financial conduct Authority has been  asked to investigate do you think they  should  well I I know nothing of the  circumstances of this alleged meal and  who went so now I I can't comment on  that if people have uh broken the rules  or done something wrong then of course  it should be investigated but I know no  evidence for that I suppose you only  know if they've broken the rules if you  investigated  yes but I don't even know this meal  occurred so I'm not the person to  cross-examine on this but I like most  people uh don't wish to see people  breaking rules and if they have they  should be investigated  um okay  um how did you feel about the latest  opinion polls that we saw from yougov  Over the week well they they was done  over the weekend we saw it um yesterday  uh tour is 17 points behind labor  well I look forward to them improving  clearly that wasn't a good poll but the  the poll that matters as people always  say who are behind in the pose is the  one that occurs when you have a general  election uh I would imagine a general  election is still a couple of years away  uh so I think a lot is going to happen  before then and I will be supporting the  government every time it does things  which raise the prosperity and freedoms  of the British people so that is surely  the way it's become more popular  yeah I'm sure that um this trust is not  going to find it mildly amusing given  that normally you do see when there's a  new leader in post they do tend to have  a polling boost in the first few weeks  don't they  well these are very exceptional times  aren't they and the the new prime  minister took over against this  background of Global Market meltdown  bombs being sold off everywhere shares  falling a lot as well as people sifted  through the the truth of what I've been  trying to tell you which is that we are  at that point where inflation is  receding as the main problem and  recession is looming and that does  require a policy change and I therefore  look forward to around in policy change  from this government not merely some tax  rate reductions but also measures to  promote more investment more capacity  more domestic energy more domestic food  because we need to tackle the balance  payments deficit and measures to get  better value out of all our public  spending so that we control the deficits  in the right way  okay it's great to talk to you we  appreciate you taking the time this  morning thank you

